Package: wayplank
Version: 1.0.0-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Neeraj Parekh <neerajparekh@outlook.com>
Installed-Size: 1886
Depends: libbamf3-2t64 (>= 0.4.0), libc6 (>= 2.38), libcairo-gobject2 (>= 1.10.0), libcairo2 (>= 1.14.0), libdbusmenu-glib4 (>= 0.4.2), libdbusmenu-gtk3-4 (>= 0.4.2), libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 (>= 2.25.2), libgee-0.8-2 (>= 0.8.3), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.44.0), libgnome-menu-3-0 (>= 3.2.0.1), libgtk-3-0t64 (>= 3.19.12), libpango-1.0-0 (>= 1.18.0), libpangocairo-1.0-0 (>= 1.14.0), libwnck-3-0 (>= 2.91.6), libx11-6 (>= 2:1.2.99.901), libxfixes3 (>= 1:5.0), libxi6 (>= 2:1.6.99.1), dconf-gsettings-backend
Conflicts: plank
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Description: Simple dock for Wayland (Plank fork with Shell-bridge tracking)
 Wayplank keeps Plank's renderer, themes and behavior, but tracks
 application windows through a companion GNOME Shell extension
 (wayplank-bridge) instead of X11-only Wnck/Bamf, so it works in
 native Wayland sessions.
